t $(-\\sqrt{3},\\frac{2\\pi }{3}).$ We note the following:\n\n- The point $(\\frac{2\\pi }{3},-\\sqrt{3})$ lies on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x.\\,✓$\n\n- The range of $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x$ is $y\\in (-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2}),$ and $y=\\frac{2\\pi }{3}$ does **not** lie within this range. $\\,\\times $\n\nTherefore, the point $(-\\sqrt{3},\\frac{2\\pi }{3})$ does **not** lie on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978414/state.json" "file_sha256" "76b000e96c2ec257e4003ff0f930edd4c8418aacb8d35bc453f4cd017455e3b3"} {"question" "q-70788" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978414/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d1e9e949959a5cdbc9bddaf72036a25a27cc953bf323c08ed9d4bb1dd8dc9047"} {"question" "q-70788" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978414/state.json" "file_sha256" "76b000e96c2ec257e4003ff0f930edd4c8418aacb8d35bc453f4cd017455e3b3"} {"question" "q-70788" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "III only"] ["text" "None"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978414/state.json" "file_sha256" "76b000e96c2ec257e4003ff0f930edd4c8418aacb8d35bc453f4cd017455e3b3"} {"question" "q-70788" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "I only"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978414/state.json" "file_sha256" "76b000e96c2ec257e40